{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ComplexDilogBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ComplexDilogBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithm","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogReflection"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.cLiTwo_reflection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.cLiTwo_reflection","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ComplexDilogBridge.lean#L122-L157","doc":"**The complex Euler reflection identity, on `ball(½, ½)`.**\n\n    Li₂ z + Li₂ (1 − z) = π²/6 − log z · log (1 − z)\n\nProved by analytic continuation from the real segment `(0,1)`, where it is\n`cLiTwo_reflection_ofReal` — itself a transport of the sorry-free real\n`LiTwo_reflection'`. This discharges the continuation step recorded as the\nremaining work in bean `qou-gkco`.\n\n**Scope.** `|z| < 1` throughout the ball, so this does *not* by itself reach\nthe 5₂ saddle root `y₁` (`|y₁| = 1.52`); that still needs the inversion\nformula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_ofReal_nhdsNE_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tendsto_ofReal_nhdsNE_half","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ComplexDilogBridge.lean#L107-L120","doc":"`ℝ → ℂ` carries the punctured neighbourhood of `½` in ℝ into the punctured\nneighbourhood of `½` in ℂ. This is what makes the real segment an accumulation\nset for the identity theorem. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.cLiTwo_reflection_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.cLiTwo_reflection_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ComplexDilogBridge.lean#L74-L92","doc":"**The Euler reflection identity on the real segment, stated in ℂ.**\n\nTransported from the sorry-free real `LiTwo_reflection'`. This is the set on\nwhich the complex reflection identity is already known — the input to an\nidentity-theorem continuation, which is the remaining work (`qou-gkco`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.cLiTwo_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.cLiTwo_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ComplexDilogBridge.lean#L54-L64","doc":"**The bridge.** `cLiTwo` at a real argument is the real `LiTwo`.\n\nUnconditional: both series are the same termwise after casting, and where\nneither converges both `tsum`s are `0` by Mathlib's junk-value convention, so\nno disc hypothesis is needed. ","signatureChunk":0}]}